---
title: Whipped Salted Caramel
yield: 541%g
---

In a #small saucepan{}, bring the @heavy cream{120%g} to a boil, then set aside.

Combine the @sugar{175%g}, @glucose syrup{30%g}, and @water{40%g} in a #saucepan{}. Heat until it caramelizes and the color becomes amber. Do not stir once it's boiling.

Remove from the heat and add the warm heavy cream in 2-3 additions. Be careful as it will bubble up. Stir gently after each addition.

Let cool to 65 C, then add the @butter{175%g}(cut in small cubes). Emulsify with a #hand blender{} (if available) or by hand with a #spatula{}.

Add the @salt{1%g} and combine with a spatula.

Let completely cool, then using a #mixer with whisk attachment{}, whip until the color becomes light and the caramel is airy and fluffy.